Original commit body from fff84f80396c83a0bd530ada31fe3012e9543dbb:

Last part of WI-pivap: a base written BARE but bound through a
namespace / package import bound any in-repo class of the same short
name, because the core linker has no import context.

- Analyzers record the hint: meta base_class_imports (bare base ->
  the import's qualified name) for PHP use, Groovy / Scala single-type
  imports and C# using aliases; meta visible_namespaces for C# (the
  enclosing namespace chain, the using namespaces, the global one).
- Groovy and Scala classes / traits / enums (Groovy interfaces too)
  record a package-qualified qualified_name, which they lacked.
- Linker: an import-bound bare base goes through the qualifier check
  (an alias looks up the import's class); a C# bare base keeps only
  candidates of a visible namespace (_namespace_fit); PHP \Foo\Bar
  bases are split on \ (they were dropped before).
- Two symbol_meta keys registered (spec 59 -> 61).

Examples: use Illuminate\...\Model; class User extends Model,
import groovy.lang.Script, import akka.actor.Actor and using System;
class E : Exception (from namespace MyApp) no longer bind the in-repo
Model / Script / Actor / MyApp.Errors.Exception.

